1. CURRENT ARCHITECTURAL FOUNDATION
============================================================

Canonical architecture:

Broker / Manual Entry
        ↓
Normalized Executions
        ↓
Supabase Execution Ledger
        ↓
Deterministic FIFO Reconstruction
        ↓
Reconstructed Trades
        ↓
Analytics / Dashboard / Trade History

Canonical rule:

Executions are the source of truth.
Trades are derived state.

Manual Entry and Edit Trade are execution producers/editors.

They must NOT become a second trade engine.

Protected systems:

- Broker sync
- Execution ledger
- FIFO reconstruction
- pairTrades
- Reconciliation
- P&L
- Analytics
- Dashboard V2
- Existing canonical lifecycle behavior

Any future improvement must preserve these boundaries.

============================================================
2. CURRENT MANUAL TRADE MODES
============================================================

COMPLETE
- Entry + Exit
- Creates entry and exit executions

PARTIAL_ENTRY
- Opening/additional execution
- One opening execution
- Position remains open

PARTIAL_EXIT
- Reduces/closes an existing manual position
- One reducing execution
- Existing contractKey is preserved

Direction semantics:

LONG
- BUY = open/add
- SELL = reduce/close

SHORT
- SELL = open/add
- BUY = reduce/close

Multiplier:

OPTIONS = 100
Other current supported asset types = 1

Manual lifecycle identity:

contractKey = MANUAL-{ticker}-{uuid}

Manual identification:

contractKey.startsWith("MANUAL-")

