1. ATOMIC EDIT TRADE PERSISTENCE
------------------------------------------------------------

Current conceptual flow:

Validate
    ↓
Delete existing execution(s)
    ↓
Create replacement execution(s)
    ↓
Save

Risk:

DELETE succeeds
    ↓
INSERT fails
    ↓
Trade can be left incomplete

Target architecture:

Validate
    ↓
BEGIN TRANSACTION
    ↓
Delete / replace execution(s)
    ↓
Insert replacement execution(s)
    ↓
COMMIT

Any failure:

ROLLBACK
    ↓
Original execution state remains intact

Implementation goals:

- Move transaction boundary to server side
- Preserve existing lifecycle semantics
- Preserve existing contractKey
- Do not modify FIFO behavior
- Do not create a parallel trade system
- Do not modify canonical execution schema unnecessarily

Priority:
CRITICAL

Estimated effort:
~1.5–2 hours initial implementation + testing

Planned substeps:

1A. Inspect current execution storage path
1B. Determine transaction boundary
1C. Implement atomic manual lifecycle replacement
1D. Connect EditTradeModal
1E. Test Complete
1F. Test Partial Entry
1G. Test Partial Exit
1H. Test rollback/failure behavior

